+.IP "\-\-allow\-command=COMMAND[,COMMAND...]"
+Only forward messages whose Xymon command appears in the case-insensitive,
+comma-separated allowlist. The option may be repeated. Command suffixes are
+normalized, so "client/local", "status+10m", and "status/group:ops" match
+"client" and "status". Typical client deployments allow "client,status,data".
+.br
+"combo" and "extcombo" are checked recursively as envelopes; every embedded
+message must be valid and allowed. "schedule" cannot be allowed because it may
+contain a command executed later. Filtering is disabled when this option is
+omitted. Dropped messages are counted in the proxy status report.
+
+.IP "\-\-hosts=FILENAME"
+Only forward messages for hosts defined in the specified
+.I hosts.cfg
+file. This is optional and independent of command filtering. It is intended
+for deployments where each proxy owns a subset of monitored hosts: point each
+proxy at a file containing only its assigned nodes to prevent it from writing
+status, data, or client messages for nodes assigned to another proxy.
+.br
+The file is parsed with Xymon's native hosts parser, including included files.
+Canonical hostnames and "CLIENT:" aliases are accepted, case-insensitively.
+Every embedded message in a "combo" or "extcombo" envelope must name an
+allowed host. The entire envelope is dropped if any hostname is absent or not
+listed. Commands without a defined status, data, or client hostname format are
+dropped while hostname checking is enabled. An unreadable or empty file causes
+the proxy to abort during startup. If this option is omitted, hostname checking
+is disabled. The proxy checks the file and all included files for updates every
+30 seconds; SIGHUP triggers an immediate check. A valid, non-empty configuration
+replaces the active hostname set atomically. If reloading fails, the proxy logs
+the error and continues using the previous configuration.
+
